<title>UK: Transco UK gas forecasts for April 18.</title>
<headline>Transco UK gas forecasts for April 18.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transco, the pipeline and transport arm of BG plc, has announced the following data and forecasts for UK gas consumption in the period April 17 to 19.</p>
<p>DEMAND</p>
<p>(mcm = millon cubic metres)</p>
<p>April 17 (actual) 223 mcm, 52 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>April 18 (forecast) 224 mcm, 52 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>April 19 (forecast) 215 mcm, 50 percent of peak day demand</p>
<p>TEMPERATURE</p>
<p>(SNT = seasonal normal temperature)</p>
<p>April 17 (actual) 8.7 Celsius, seasonal normal 9.7 Celsius</p>
<p>April 18 (forecast) 8.5 Celsius, seasonal normal 9.9 Celsius</p>
<p>April 19 (forecast) 6.9 Celsius, seasonal normal 6.9 Celsius</p>
<p>There was no supply interruption called on Friday, with none expected on Saturday</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
</text>
